@title what you mean by fighting, and how far you take it
@see style protect skills

  stance [<stance>]

Your stance says which part you play in a fight: 'aggressive',
'defensive', 'supportive' or 'any'. With no argument it tells you
which one you are on.

Some effects can only be used from a particular stance, and they
change it for you when they need to. That is why you cannot change
it twice in a row: five minutes have to pass between one change and
the next.

  combat [<mode>]

The mode is lethal or non-lethal. In a non-lethal fight, whoever is
about to fall stops at one hit point, you both stop fighting, and
the practice ends there. In a lethal one, they die.

The mode that counts is the one of whoever lands the last blow.
